# 📚 Study Resource Sharing Platform

## 🚀 Overview

The **Study Resource Sharing Platform (StudyHub)** is a full-stack web application where students can upload, share, and access study materials such as notes, PDFs, and useful links.

It is built using **HTML, Bootstrap, JavaScript, Node.js, Express, and MongoDB**.

---

## ✨ Features

* 🔐 User Authentication (Signup & Login)
* 📤 Upload study resources:

  * 📄 PDF files
  * 🔗 Links
  * 📝 Notes
* 📚 View all uploaded resources
* 🔍 Search by subject/title
* 🗑️ Delete resources (Admin / Owner only)
* 👤 User profile dropdown
* 📁 File upload using Multer

---

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

### Frontend

* HTML
* CSS (Bootstrap)
* JavaScript

### Backend

* Node.js
* Express.js

### Database

* MongoDB (Local)

---

## ⚙️ Installation & Setup

### 1️⃣ Clone the repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/study-resource-sharing-platform.git
cd study-resource-sharing-platform
```

---

### 2️⃣ Install dependencies

```bash
cd backend
npm install
```

---

### 3️⃣ Setup MongoDB (Local)

Make sure MongoDB is installed and running.

Connection used:

```bash
mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017/studyhub
```

---

### 4️⃣ Run the server

```bash
node server.js
```

Server runs at:

```
http://localhost:3000
```

---

### 5️⃣ Open frontend

Open in browser:

* `login.html`
* `signup.html`
* `dashboard.html`
* `upload.html`

---

